      "text": "## The Big Picture: Time Organization Hierarchy"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-RHYTHM-METER.md#002",
      "path": [
        "03-RHYTHM-METER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:music-theory:03-rhythm-meter, git-history:music-theory:03-rhythm-meter]",
        "canonical_path": "music-theory/03-RHYTHM-METER.md",
        "concepts": "[rhythm, meter]",
        "current_path": "music-theory/03-RHYTHM-METER.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:rhythm-meter",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rhythm, meter]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rhythm and Meter",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTEMPO (BPM)\n│  The absolute rate — how fast is the pulse?\n│  ♩= 60 = 1 beat/second; ♩= 120 = 2 beats/second\n│\n├── BEAT UNIT (the \"pulse\" note value)\n│   Quarter note (♩), half note (♩♩), eighth note (♪) — context dependent\n│\n├── METER = how beats group\n│   │\n│   ├── SIMPLE METER: each beat divides into 2\n│   │   2/4 = 2 beats of ♩ each    (march)\n│   │   3/4 = 3 beats of ♩ each    (waltz)\n│   │   4/4 = 4 beats of ♩ each    (most common)\n│   │\n│   └── COMPOUND METER: each beat divides into 3\n│       6/8  = 2 beats of dotted-♩ each    (each beat = ♪♪♪)\n│       9/8  = 3 beats of dotted-♩ each\n│       12/8 = 4 beats of dotted-♩ each\n│\n├── SUBDIVISION: how beat units divide\n│   Simple duple: ♩ → ♪♪ (2 eighths per quarter)\n│   Simple triple: ♩ → ♪♪♪ (but this makes it compound)\n│   Triplets: 3 equal notes in the space of 2 (♩ triplet = 3 in space of 2)\n│\n└── PHRASE / HYPERMETER: how measures group\n    Common: 2, 4, 8, 16-bar phrase units\n    Irregular: 5, 7, 11 bars (Brubeck, Bartók, Balkan music)\n```"
    },
    {
